{
  "title": "Lateral Patellar Compression Syndrome",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/knee-and-sports/3021/lateral-patellar-compression-syndrome",
  "subtitle": "Updated: May 29 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Lateral patellar compression syndrome is the improper tracking of the patella in the trochlear groove generally caused by a tight lateral retinaculum.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made clinically with pain with compression of the patella and moderate lateral facet tenderness and sunrise knee radiographs will often show patellar tilt in the lateral direction.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is nonoperative with physical therapy focusing on quadriceps stretching and strengthening. Operative lateral retinaculum release is indicated in refractory cases.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Mechanism",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Caused by **tight lateral retinaculum**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "leads to excessive **lateral tilt** without excessive patellar mobility",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**Miserable Triad**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "is a term coined for anatomic characteristics that lead to an increased Q angle and an exacerbation of patellofemoral dysplasia. They include:",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**femoral anteversion**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**genu valgum**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**external tibial torsion / pronated feet**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Presentation",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "pain with stair climbing",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**theatre sign** (pain with sitting for long periods of time)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "pain with compression of patella and moderate lateral facet tenderness",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "inability to evert the lateral edge of the patella",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "patellar tilt in lateral direction",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "NSAIDS, activity modification, and therapy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "mainstay of treatment and should be done for extensive period of time",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "technique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "therapy should emphasize **vastus medialis strengthening** and **closed chain short arc quadriceps exercises**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "arthroscopic lateral release",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "objective evidence of **lateral tilting** (neutral or negative tilt)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3021/images/merchants%20min%20tilt_moved.jpg",
                          "caption": ""
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "pain refractory to extensive rehabilitation",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "inability to evert the lateral edge of the patella",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "ideal candidate has no symptoms of instability",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "medial patellar glide of less than one quadrant",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "lateral patellar glide of less than three quadrants",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "patellar realignment surgery",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**Maquet (**tubercle anteriorization)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "indicated only for distal pole lesions",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "only elevate 1 cm or else risk of skin necrosis",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**Elmslie-Trillat (medialization)**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "indicated only for instability with lateral translation (not isolated lateral tilt)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "avoid if medial patellar facet arthrosis",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**Fulkerson alignment surgery** (tubercle anteriorization and medialization)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "indications (controversial)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "lateral and distal pole lesions",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "-1",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "increased Q angle",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "-1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "contraindications",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "**superior medial arthrosis** (scope before you perform the surgery)",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "-1",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "skeletal immaturity",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "-1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Techniques",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Arthroscopic lateral release**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "technique",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "viewing through superior portal will show medial facet does not articulate with trochlea at 40 degrees of knee flexion",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "be sure adequate hemostasis is obtained",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "postoperatively the patella should be able to be **passively tilted 80°**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "complications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "persistent or worsened pain",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "patellar instability with medial translation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
